  # =================================================================
  #  Passage outline, from the sketch in sketch/C10.ee.xvi.
  #
  #  Walls are the OUTERMOST strokes, black or red. Each stroke is put
  #  on the ceiling or the floor by its mean offset from the centreline;
  #  then WITHIN EACH SIDE SEPARATELY the points are binned by x at
  #  0.44 m and the outermost taken -- highest for ceiling, lowest for
  #  floor. Bins a side does not cover are interpolated across.
  #
  #  Doing it per side is the whole trick. Built from all points at
  #  once, 31% of bins contain no floor stroke, so the "lowest point"
  #  there is a ceiling point and the floor line leaps to the roof and
  #  back once per bin -- a sawtooth down the whole elevation.
  #
  #  Two near-vertical red strokes spanning 9 m and 13 m are the cliff
  #  faces at the entrances, not passage wall; inside the envelope they
  #  spike each end of the profile. Drawn separately below as slope
  #  lines, matching the cliff on the plan. Anything taller than 6 m
  #  cannot be passage here -- the cave's vertical range is 4 m.
  #
  #  Smoothed once only; a profile carries real detail.
  #  Checked: floor stays 0.71-5.35 m below the ceiling, no crossings.
  # =================================================================

